Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 07:01:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: configure session picker sorting

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Let users choose how the /sessions picker orders sessions.
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none

Patch intent:
Add display.session_picker_sort with recent, created, and name modes. Apply it
consistently to loaded sessions, filtered rows, saved sessions, and both picker
caches.

Why it exists:
The picker defaulted to recent activity with no user-visible choice, while saved
and server sections can make the effective ordering difficult to navigate.

Upstream integration points:
DisplayConfig defines the persisted setting. The session picker loading and
filtering paths own ordering, and its memory and disk caches key cached results
by the chosen mode.

Update guidance:
Preserve recent as the default and route every session list ordering path through
the shared comparator. Update cache keys when adding a new sort-dependent view.

Validation:
cargo test -p jcode-config-types session_picker_sort_defaults_to_recent_and_accepts_named_orders --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui session_sort_orders_by_the_configured_field --lib
cargo test -p jcode-tui cached_grouped_sessions_round_trip_from_disk --lib
